{
  "id": "c2-extension-generator-controls",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Does a matching decoder recover the planted message?",
  "question": "Do matching source decoder rules recover known planted text across the eight C2-EXT generator-and-plant pairs when supplied the correct key?",
  "reader_question": "Can a decoding tool miss the right message even with the right key?",
  "summary": "Matching the decoder to the planted rule raises median recovery from 10–33% to 98–100% across eight source generator-and-plant pairs. All source recovery gates pass.",
  "finding": "All eight seven-seed source gates pass. Six paired-skip generator pairs have 100% median recovery; two drift plants have 98.33%. Baseline keyskip1 medians range from 10% to 32.92%. All 112 replay score/recovery values exactly match archived source; minimum matching-rule seed recovery is 96.25%.",
  "reader_finding": "With the right key supplied, a decoder that matches the planted rule recovered 98–100% of runes at the median; the comparison decoder recovered 10–33%.",
  "reader_limit": "This checks a decoding tool on planted messages. It does not search manuscript keys, test nonzero offsets, or establish native generator runtime parity.",
  "limitations": "Finite known-key English-derived plants at 240 runes; seven fixed seeds per pair. No wrong-key calibration or manuscript sweep. Exact Welsh corpus and I2 panel model are missing for the target sweep. Source generator models are not tested against native runtimes. A5 uses offset zero despite its source label. Independent score rescoring uses disclosed 1e-12 summation tolerance; direct source replay matches exactly.",
  "next_steps": "Test any proposed manuscript search with matched wrong-key/search-maximum controls and exact source inputs before interpreting its output.",
  "outcome": "supported",
  "tags": [
    "source control",
    "decoder recovery",
    "key skipping",
    "generator models",
    "known key",
    "drift",
    "skipping two key draws",
    "two-draw rejection",
    "paired skip"
  ],
